[32m+[m[32mA JWT lasts 15 minutes. The portal rotates it automatically with `POST /api/session/rotate` before expiry (about ten minutes after issue). Rotation sets a new signed cookie and invalidates the previous token ID (JTI), so replay of the old cookie is rejected. A session has an eight-hour absolute maximum lifetime; rotation cannot extend it beyond that cap. Signing out revokes the in-memory session and clears the cookie with matching `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, path, and SameSite attributes. Missing, malformed, modified, expired, logged-out, and superseded cookies receive a generic `401 Unauthorized`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe session registry and limiter use in-memory state for a single local process. Restarting the app invalidates active demo sessions and resets counters. They are intentionally not durable or shared between multiple servers; a real multi-instance application would need a shared store such as Redis and a reviewed key/rotation policy.[m
