[32m+[m[32m# Task 3 — Cryptographic Session Security Plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Scope and security behavior[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mContinue the existing loopback-only TypeScript/Express demo and preserve Task 2’s SQLite-backed BOLA authorization. Replace browser-readable bearer-token storage with an HMAC-SHA256-signed JWT carried only in an `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite=Lax` session cookie for the local lab. The browser must not write authentication tokens or profile data to `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`; it will request the current account from a cookie-authenticated endpoint after each page load. Explain that HttpOnly prevents JavaScript from reading the token but does not make XSS harmless: injected same-origin script could still issue authenticated actions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe session API will verify demo credentials, set a 15-minute JWT cookie, return only non-secret status/account data, support cookie-based session inspection, explicit token rotation and sign-out, and reject missing, invalid, expired, replayed, or superseded session IDs without exposing cryptographic details. The session registry is process-local and exists to enforce single-use rotation and logout in this training demo; it is not durable or horizontally distributed. Tokens are HS256, validated with an explicit algorithm allowlist, issuer, audience, subject, session ID, JTI and expiry. Rotation issues a new JTI, invalidates the previous JTI, and retains an eight-hour absolute session cap.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAdd an in-memory sliding-window limiter with independent per-IP login throttling and per-IP-plus-session throttling for protected record requests. The login limit is five attempts per minute; protected-record requests are limited to ten per minute per IP/session key. Return `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `X-RateLimit-Reset`; blocked requests return `429` and `Retry-After`. Do not trust caller-supplied `X-Forwarded-For` while bound directly to loopback. The in-memory limiter is intentionally single-process and resets on restart; document Redis as the scale-out option rather than adding an external service to this Kali lab.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Implementation map[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/auth.ts`: issue/verify short-lived HS256 tokens containing `sub`, `email`, `sid`, and unique `jti`; expose TTL and absolute maximum lifetime constants.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/sessionStore.ts`: keep active session families/JTIs in process memory, atomically rotate JTIs, enforce the absolute lifetime, and revoke on logout.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/rateLimit.ts`: implement a bounded in-memory sliding-window counter and Express middleware/header behavior.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/middleware/requireSession.ts`: read the named JWT only from the cookie, verify all claims and active session state, and fail closed with a generic 401.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/routes/session.ts`: login, current-session inspection, one-time rotation, and logout; set/clear the HttpOnly Secure SameSite cookie with a fixed path and expiry.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/routes/records.ts`: retain the parameterized `(record ID, verified owner ID)` query and add the per-IP/session limiter.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `src/app.ts`: wire cookie parsing, session registry, login throttling, cookie-only protected routes, and no-store headers.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `public/app.js`: remove all Web Storage token/profile reads and writes and Authorization headers; rely on same-origin cookies, `/api/session`, `/api/session/rotate`, and logout; refresh the in-memory view from the server after reload.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `tests/records.test.ts`: prove cookie flags, absence of Web Storage token persistence, no token in JSON, valid and invalid cookies, token rotation/replay denial, expiry, logout, header values, and sliding-window 429 behavior, while retaining BOLA access tests.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `README.md`: document Web Storage/XSS risks and limits, cookie attributes, rotation/expiry, rate limits/headers, local cURL/browser demonstrations, and loopback-only limitations.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReuse the existing Northstar portal design. Do not add decorative assets or change the visual identity for this security-focused update. Preserve `127.0.0.1` as the shipped host default and the local SQLite fixture set. A separately explicit `BOLAGUARD_HOST=0.0.0.0` override is permitted only for the isolated Cloud Preview listener; do not put it in the learner's local template or use it on Kali. The explicit cookie SameSite setting defaults to `lax` for the requested local exercise; public HTTPS embedded Preview needs `SameSite=None; Secure`, so expose a deliberate `BOLAGUARD_COOKIE_SAME_SITE` configuration rather than inferring it from internal request scheme or `NODE_ENV`. Keep local setup defaulted to `lax`.[m
